"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/258/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"258E - Little Elephant and Tree"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Very useful thing in this problem is ordering all vertices in DFS order (preorped). After that any subtree can be represented as a some sequence of continuous vertices. Consider that we have some fixed vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Which vertices should be included in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"? Obviously, if in the path from the root to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is some non-empty vertex (i. e. such that has at least one integer in its list) than each vertex from substree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" should be included in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", but since we now working with preorder traversal of the tree, we consider that every vertex from some segment ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] must be included to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". More generally, let for each vertex keep some set of segments ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":";"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). If on the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th operation we have two vertices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we add segment ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":";"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") to vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":";"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") to vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also for each vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1.."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") we add segment ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":";"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":";"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") is a segment in our preored traversal for subtree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". After that, you can see that, if we unite all segments from all vertices on the path from the root to some vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we find the result for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", which will be the size of the resulting set."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So now we need some data structure that would support three operations: add(l, r), subtract(l, r), count(). The first one should add 1 to all positions from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive. The second should subtract 1 from all positions from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive. The last should count the number of non-zero element. This all can be done either with segment tree or sqrt-decomposition."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.